OL,3,ASignificant drop in levels of toxic
OL,4,A'forever' chemicals in England's rivers
OL,5,
OL,6,FLevels of the two most toxic "forever"
OL,7,Fchemicals in England's rivers have
OL,8,Fdropped by nearly a third over the last
OL,9,Fdecade, according to new figures from
OL,10,Fthe Environment Agency (EA).
OL,12,FThe decline in the chemicals, PFOS and
OL,13,FPFOA, has been put down to stricter
OL,14,Frestrictions on their use in products
OL,15,Fafter increasing evidence emerged of
OL,16,Ftheir damaging impact on human health
OL,17,Fand the environment.
OL,19,FOne expert studying the impact of the
OL,20,Fchemicals said it was "brilliant" to
OL,21,Fsee how far the UK has come on this
OL,22,Fissue.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,0,100
